 a - 2a\u00b2 c ] / (8h (c + a ) )\n\n= [8h\u00b2 a - 2a\u00b2 c ] / (8h (c + a ) )\n\nTherefore, equation:\n\n(a h ) / (2c + a ) = [8h\u00b2 a - 2a\u00b2 c ] / (8h (c + a ) )\n\nMultiply both sides by (2c + a ) * 8h (c + a ):\n\n8h (c + a ) * a h = [8h\u00b2 a - 2a\u00b2 c ] * (2c + a )\n\nLeft side: 8a h\u00b2 (c + a )\n\nRight side: (8h\u00b2 a - 2a\u00b2 c )(2c + a )\n\nExpand the right side:\n\n= 8h\u00b2 a * 2c + 8h\u00b2 a * a - 2a\u00b2 c * 2c - 2a\u00b2 c * a\n\n= 16h\u00b2 a c + 8h\u00b2 a\u00b2 - 4a\u00b2 c\u00b2 - 2a\u00b3 c\n\nThus, equation:\n\n8a h\u00b2 (c + a ) = 16h\u00b2 a c + 8h\u00b2 a\u00b2 - 4a\u00b2 c\u00b2 - 2a\u00b3 c\n\nDivide both sides by a:\n\n8 h\u00b2 (c + a ) = 16h\u00b2 c + 8h\u00b2 a - 4a c\u00b2 - 2a\u00b2 c\n\nSimplify left side: 8h\u00b2 c + 8h\u00b2 a\n\nRight side: 16h\u00b2 c + 8h\u00b2 a - 4a c\u00b2 - 2a\u00b2 c\n\nSubtract left side from both sides:\n\n0 = 8h\u00b2 c - 4a c\u00b2 - 2a\u00b2 c\n\nFactor out 4c:\n\n0 = 4c(2h\u00b2 - a c - (a\u00b2 / 2 ) )\n\nBut this seems complicated. Let's substitute c in terms of a and h. Recall that in the isoceles triangle, c = sqrt( (a/2 )\u00b2 + h\u00b2 )\n\nLet\u2019s set c\u00b2 = (a\u00b2 /4 ) + h\u00b2\n\nThen, the equation becomes:\n\n0 = 4c(2h\u00b2 - a c - (a\u00b2 / 2 ) )\n\nBut this would require 2h\u00b2 - a c - (a\u00b2 / 2 ) = 0\n\n=> 2h\u00b2 = a c + (a\u00b2 ) / 2\n\nBut c = sqrt( a\u00b2/4 + h\u00b2 )\n\nSubstitute:\n\n2h\u00b2 = a sqrt( a\u00b2/4 + h\u00b2 ) + a\u00b2 / 2\n\nThis is a complicated equation. Let's square both sides to eliminate the square root.\n\nFirst, isolate the sqrt term:\n\n2h\u00b2 - a\u00b2 / 2 = a sqrt( a\u00b2/4 + h\u00b2 )\n\nSquare both sides:\n\n(2h\u00b2 - a\u00b2 / 2 )\u00b2 = a\u00b2 (a\u00b2/4 + h\u00b2 )\n\nExpand left side:\n\n= 4h^4 - 2 * 2h\u00b2 * (a\u00b2 / 2 ) + (a\u00b2 / 2 )\u00b2\n\n= 4h^4 - 2a\u00b2 h\u00b2 + a^4 /4\n\nRight side:\n\n= a\u00b2 (a\u00b2 /4 + h\u00b2 ) = a^4 /4 + a\u00b2 h\u00b2\n\nSet equal:\n\n4h^4 - 2a\u00b2