3 hours by balancing car usage and walking.\n\n**Detailed Steps:**\n\n1. **Phase 1: Car Travel and Initial Drop-off**\n   - **Time (t\u2081):** A and B drive the car for \\( t\u2081 \\) hours, covering \\( 50t\u2081 \\) km.\n   - **C's Position:** C walks \\( 5t\u2081 \\) km during this time.\n\n2. **Phase 2: Car Return to Pick Up C**\n   - **Distance to Close:** After dropping A off, B drives back towards C. The gap is \\( 50t\u2081 - 5t\u2081 = 45t\u2081 \\) km.\n   - **Relative Speed:** Closing at \\( 50 + 5 = 55 \\) km/h. Time to meet: \\( t\u2082 = \\frac{45t\u2081}{55} = \\frac{9}{11}t\u2081 \\).\n\n3. **Phase 3: Final Leg to Destination**\n   - **Meeting Point:** After time \\( t\u2082 \\), B and C meet at \\( 5t\u2081 + 5t\u2082 \\) km from start.\n   - **Remaining Distance:** \\( 62 - 5(t\u2081 + t\u2082) \\) km. Time to drive this: \\( t\u2083 = \\frac{62 - 5(t\u2081 + t\u2082)}{50} \\).\n\n4. **Total Time Calculation:**\n   - **Total Time (T):** \\( T = t\u2081 + t\u2082 + t\u2083 \\).\n   - Substitute \\( t\u2082 = \\frac{9}{11}t\u2081 \\):\n     \\[\n     T = t\u2081 + \\frac{9}{11}t\u2081 + \\frac{62 - 5\\left(t\u2081 + \\frac{9}{11}t\u2081\\right)}{50} = \\frac{20}{11}t\u2081 + \\frac{62 - \\frac{100}{11}t\u2081}{50}\n     \\]\n     Simplifying yields \\( T = \\frac{18}{11}t\u2081 + \\frac{31}{25} \\).\n\n5. **A's Walking Time Constraint:**\n   - A walks the remaining \\( 62 - 50t\u2081 \\) km. Time required: \\( \\frac{62 - 50t\u2081}{5} \\).\n   - Total time for A: \\( t\u2081 + \\frac{62 - 50t\u2081}{5} \\leq T \\).\n\n6. **Solving for \\( t\u2081 \\):**\n   - Combining constraints leads to \\( t\u2081 \\geq \\frac{3069}{2925} \\approx 1.049 \\) hours.\n   - Substituting back, total time \\( T \\approx 2.956 \\) hours (\u22482h57.5m), which is under 3 hours.\n\n**Verification:**\n- **A's Journey:** Rides to ~52.45 km, then walks ~9.55 km, totaling \u22482.959 hours.\n- **B & C's Journey:** Drive, return, and final trip also total \u22482.956 hours.\n\n**Conclusion:** Yes, all three can reach the 62 km point in **less than 3 hours** using optimal car shuttling strategy.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{Yes}", "ground_truth_solution": "\n\nWe want to determine whether A, B, and C can reach a point 62 km away in less than 3 hours using the given parameters: they can each walk at 5 km/hr and can use a car that travels at 50 km/hr and can carry any two of them at once.\n\n1. **Initial Driving Phase**:\n    - A and B drive a distance of 53 km at 50 km/hr.\n    - Time taken: \n    \\[\n    \\text{Time} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Speed}} = \\frac{53 \\text{ km}}{50 \\text{ km/hr}} = 1.06 \\text{ hours}\n    \\]\n\n2. **B Walking Phase**:\n    - After traveling 53 km, B gets out and walks the remaining 9 km to the destination.\n    - B's walking speed: 5 km/hr.\n    - Time taken for B to walk 9 km:\n    \\[\n    \\text{Time} = \\frac{9 \\text{ km}}{5 \\text{ km/hr}} = 1.80 \\text{ hours}\n    \\]\n    - Total time for B to arrive: \n    \\[\n    1.06 \\text{ hours (in car)} + 1.80 \\text{ hours (walking)} = 2.86 \\text{ hours}\n    \\]\n\n3. **C Walking Phase**:\n    - While A and B are driving, C is walking towards the destination.\n    - Time for C to engage:\n    \\[\n    1.06 \\text{ hours}\n    \\]\n    - Distance covered by C in this time:\n    \\[\n    \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} = 5 \\text{ km/hr} \\times 1.06 \\text{ hours} = 5.30 \\text{ km}\n    \\]\n\n4. **A Returning to Pick Up C**:\n    - A continues driving to return and pick up C.\n    - Distance A drives back to meet C:\n    \\[\n    \\text{Distance to meet C} = 9.5 \\text{ km}\n    \\]\n    - Time taken for A to drive back:\n    \\[\n    \\text{Time} = \\frac{9.5 \\text{ km}}{50 \\text{ km/hr}} = 0.19 \\text{ hours}\n    \\]\n\n5. **C Waiting Time**:\n    - By the time A returns to pick up C, the total time elapsed is:\n    \\[\n    1.06 \\text{ hours (initial driving)} + 0.19 \\text{ hours (returning)} = 1.25 \\text{ hours}\n 