n\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix}\n-4 & -4 & 4 \\\\\n1 & -9 & 15 \\\\\n5 & 11 & -5 \\\\\n\\end{vmatrix}\n\\]\n\nCompute this 3x3 determinant:\n\n= -4 * [(-9)(-5) - 15*11] - (-4) * [1*(-5) - 15*5] + 4 * [1*11 - (-9)*5]\n\nLet me compute each term step by step.\n\nFirst term: -4 * [45 - 165] = -4 * (-120) = 480\n\nSecond term: -(-4) * [ -5 - 75 ] = 4 * (-80) = -320\n\nThird term: 4 * [11 + 45] = 4 * 56 = 224\n\nAdding these up: 480 - 320 + 224 = (480 - 320) + 224 = 160 + 224 = 384\n\nTherefore, det(Minor_12) = 384\n\nNow moving to det(Minor_13):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix}\n1 & 0 & 9 & 5 \\\\\n1 & 4 & 5 & 9 \\\\\n1 & 9 & 0 & 20 \\\\\n1 & 5 & 20 & 0 \\\\\n\\end{vmatrix}\n\\]\n\nAgain, let's perform row operations to simplify. Subtract Row1 from Rows 2, 3, 4.\n\nRow2' = Row2 - Row1: (1-1, 4-0, 5-9, 9-5) \u2192 (0, 4, -4, 4)\n\nRow3' = Row3 - Row1: (1-1, 9-0, 0-9, 20-5) \u2192 (0, 9, -9, 15)\n\nRow4' = Row4 - Row1: (1-1, 5-0, 20-9, 0-5) \u2192 (0, 5, 11, -5)\n\nSo the matrix becomes:\n\nRow1: [1, 0, 9, 5]\n\nRow2: [0, 4, -4, 4]\n\nRow3: [0, 9, -9, 15]\n\nRow4: [0, 5, 11, -5]\n\nNow, expanding along the first column, which has three zeros, the determinant is:\n\n1 * det(minor 11) - 0 + 0 - 0 = determinant of the 3x3 matrix:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix}\n4 & -4 & 4 \\\\\n9 & -9 & 15 \\\\\n5 & 11 & -5 \\\\\n\\end{vmatrix}\n\\]\n\nCompute this determinant:\n\n= 4 * [(-9)(-5) - 15*11] - (-4) * [9*(-5) - 15*5] + 4 * [9*11 - (-9)*5]\n\nFirst term: 4 * [45 - 165] = 4*(-120) = -480\n\nSecond term: -(-4) * [ -45 - 75 ] = 4*(-120) = -480\n\nWait, wait, let me re-express:\n\nSecond term: -(-4) * [9*(-5) - 15*5] = 4 * [ -45 -75 ] = 4*(-120) = -480\n\nThird term: 4 * [99 +45] = 4*144 = 576\n\nAdding these up: -480 -480 + 576 = (-960) + 576 = -384\n\nTherefore, det(Minor_13) = -384\n\nWait, but determinant calculations can be tricky. Let me verify once again:\n\nFirst term: 4*(45 - 165) = 4*(-120) = -480\n\nSecond term: -(-4)*( -45 -75 ) = 4*(-120) = -480\n\nThird term: 4*(99 +45) = 4*144 = 576\n\nTotal